# Project-root .env for `docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml -f
# docker/docker-compose.prod.yml ...` on the clinic Server PC ONLY.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the repo root and fill in the real value(s).
# `.env` itself is gitignored - never commit it.
#
# This is separate from `backend/.env` (the FastAPI app's own settings,
# loaded via `env_file:` inside the containers) - this root-level `.env` is
# read by the `docker compose` CLI itself, for variable substitution inside
# the compose YAML files (the `${...}` references in docker-compose.prod.yml).

# Must match the actual password already set on the live `postgres` role
# inside the volume named by POSTGRES_VOLUME_NAME below - changing this
# value here does NOT change the real database password (see
# docker-compose.prod.yml's comments for why). Get the current real value
# from whoever manages the clinic server; do not invent a new one without
# also rotating it in Postgres itself first.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Optional overrides - both already default to the real clinic Server PC
# address (192.168.68.106) inside docker-compose.prod.yml, so these only
# need to be set here if deploying to a different machine/IP.
# CLINIC_FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://192.168.68.106:3000
# CLINIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.68.106:8000/api/v1

# --- Production volume identity - REQUIRED, no default, never guess ---
#
# docker-compose.prod.yml declares postgres_data/redis_data/backend_var_data
# as `external: true` - Compose will NEVER create, rename, or recreate
# these; it only ever attaches to a volume that already exists under
# EXACTLY the name given here, and refuses outright (a normal Compose
# error, no destructive action) if that name doesn't exist. This is
# deliberate: a fresh install and an already-running clinic install must
# never be able to silently diverge into "Compose quietly made a new empty
# database" just because these three lines were left unset or guessed at.
#
# Find this machine's REAL, already-existing volume names before ever
# setting these - do not assume, do not copy another clinic's values:
#
#     docker volume ls
#
# Then set all three to exactly what that command shows for THIS machine.
# There is no safe generic default - a hardcoded default here would either
# be meaningless for a fresh install or, worse, silently point an existing
# clinic's data at the wrong volume if their real names ever differ from
# whatever default was guessed. Leaving any of these unset makes
# `docker compose` (and therefore `deploy.cmd`) refuse to run at all,
# rather than fabricate a value - see docker-compose.prod.yml's own
# comments for exactly why.
POSTGRES_VOLUME_NAME=
REDIS_VOLUME_NAME=
BACKEND_VAR_VOLUME_NAME=
